.TH WINZBUF 1
.SH NAME
winzbuf \- which window owns each cell of the screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/winzbuf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I WinZBuf
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/WinZBuf.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
TempleOS keeps one entry per character cell of the screen naming the
window that owns it, and compositing is a lookup in that array rather
than a walk of a window list.  The original plots it one pixel to the
cell, so the picture in the corner is a little map of the desktop: move a
window and its patch moves.
.PP
.IR wm (1)
has no equivalent to expose \- an Inferno client sees only its own image
\- so this port owns the windows it maps.  Drag the three panes and the
map below them updates the same way.  The idea is the original's; the
scope is one window instead of the display.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B LMB
Drag a pane
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/winzbuf.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
